      "We go deeper on this in [how AI assistants choose which businesses to recommend](/blog/how-ai-assistants-choose-businesses).",
      "## What AI SEO work includes",
      "### 1. Make your business information consistent everywhere",
      "Start with your Google Business Profile, then make sure the same name, phone, website and service area appear on Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp and the directories that matter in your trade. For GTA home services, that often includes HomeStars and Houzz. Microsoft's Bing data feeds several AI tools, and Apple's data powers Siri and Apple Maps, so these listings matter more than many businesses realize. Our [Google Business Profile guide](/blog/google-business-profile-optimization) is a good place to start.",
      "### 2. Write content that answers questions directly",
      "AI assistants build answers from passages that clearly respond to a question. A sentence like 'We repair and replace asphalt shingle roofs across Richmond Hill, Vaughan and Aurora, and most leak repairs are done within two days of the inspection' is far more useful to an AI than 'We pride ourselves on quality craftsmanship.'",
      "Give each service its own page. Answer the questions customers ask on every estimate. Add a short FAQ section to key pages, written in plain language.",
      "### 3. Add structured data",
      "Structured data, or schema markup, is code that labels your information for machines: this is a local business, these are its services, this is its service area, these are frequently asked questions. It removes guesswork for both search engines and AI tools. See [schema markup explained](/blog/schema-markup-explained).",
      "### 4. Let AI crawlers read your site",
      "Some websites accidentally block the crawlers AI tools use to find content. Check that your robots.txt file isn't blocking search crawlers such as Googlebot, Bingbot, OAI-SearchBot (used for ChatGPT search) or PerplexityBot. Some sites also publish an llms.txt file, a newer and still-evolving convention for summarizing a site for AI tools. Read more in [what is llms.txt](/blog/what-is-llms-txt).",
      "### 5. Earn reviews and mentions",
      "Reviews are some of the strongest evidence an AI can find, especially detailed ones. Beyond reviews, look for real-world mentions: membership in a trade association such as HRAI for HVAC contractors, RenoMark for renovators, your local chamber of commerce, manufacturer dealer listings, sponsorships, and local news coverage. Each one is another independent source saying you exist and do good work. See [why Google reviews matter in the age of AI search](/blog/google-reviews-and-ai-search).",
      "## How to measure AI visibility",
      "Unlike classic search rankings, there's no single position to track. The practical approach is to regularly ask the main assistants the questions your customers ask, such as 'best furnace repair in Vaughan' or 'who installs heat pumps in Markham', and record whether you're mentioned, how you're described, and which sources are cited. Over time, you can see whether your visibility is improving and which competitors keep showing up.",
      "![A business owner reviewing a report of AI search mentions on a laptop in a small office](/blog/img/what-is-ai-seo-2.webp \"Track where you're mentioned across AI assistants, and which competitors show up instead.\")",
