      "Ask ChatGPT 'Who's a good plumber in Vaughan for a sump pump install?' and you'll usually get a short answer naming two to five businesses, often with a sentence about each. Ask Perplexity or Gemini and you'll get something similar, sometimes with links to where the information came from.",
      "Those few names get a huge share of attention. So how does an AI assistant decide who makes the list? It can't drive past your shop, call your office or look at your work. It relies entirely on what it can read about you online. That's good news, because most of what it reads is something you can influence.",
      "## Where AI assistants get their information",
      "Each tool works a little differently, and none publishes its exact method, but they draw on the same kinds of sources:",
